WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.160
- You look so different
in all the things you do,

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.920
like Hunger Games, Vikings.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.610
Everything you do, you look so different.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:07.443
That's so cool.

00:00:07.443 --> 00:00:08.276
You're a chameleon.

00:00:08.276 --> 00:00:09.470
- Awww, thank you so much.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.340
I mean especially for this,

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.190
like we're showing an arc
between when he's a young man

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.343
to up until he's 40 or something
with three or four kids.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.710
I always like to switch it up if I can.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.060
Actually I had a gift for you.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.020
I was gonna bring this great necklace

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.317
and a box of chocolates, but I think--

00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:29.796
(Whitney laughing drowns out Alexander)

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:32.018
- But I was like, "Maybe not."

00:00:32.018 --> 00:00:33.176
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:33.176 --> 00:00:34.009
You're funny.

00:00:34.009 --> 00:00:34.920
- It was really nice, but...

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.230
- So wait, you also like
Nashville a lot, too,

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.292
because you're releasing
a country song, right?

00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:40.125
- I am.

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:40.958
- Yes, you're working

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:41.791
on a record.
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:42.624
- [Whitney] Wow.

00:00:42.624 --> 00:00:43.693
- [Kelly] So tell everybody.

00:00:43.693 --> 00:00:44.526
- [Whitney] That's so cool.

00:00:44.526 --> 00:00:45.428
- [Alexander] Thank you.

00:00:45.428 --> 00:00:46.261
- [Kelly] Tell everybody about it.

00:00:46.261 --> 00:00:47.094
- [Whitney] Wow.

00:00:47.094 --> 00:00:47.927
- Awww, thank you.

00:00:47.927 --> 00:00:49.080
I really appreciate it.
- I love it.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.370
You sent this song, and I love it.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.820
I love that you sound country.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.290
I feel like a lot of country music now

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.380
is starting to depart

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.830
from what actual country
music sounds like.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.270
- I love traditional country music.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.630
I grew up listening to
the likes of George Strait

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.623
and everyone from that era.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.230
Randomly, I had some time off of Vikings,

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.063
and I got on a plane,

00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:08.260
and I was like, I'm gonna go to Nashville

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.270
and I'm gonna try to figure it out.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.210
I had no plan whatsoever,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.060
and while I was getting on the plane,

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:19.730
all these guys in black
attire come up to me.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.240
I was like, these guys gotta be a band.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.010
And he goes, "Hey man, I'm a
huge fan of Lone Survivor,"

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.710
which was a film I did awhile ago.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.110
He's like, "What are
you doing in Nashville?"

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.550
And I was like, "Well,
I'm trying to figure out

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.780
how to do this country thing.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.330
I wanna learn what it
takes to write a great song

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.890
and start from the ground up."

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.040
Turns out, they've played with you before.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.560
It's Tully Kennedy and Kurt Allison,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.950
who play with Jason Aldean.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.783
- Great band.

00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:43.616
- They're amazing.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.110
So they've been producing me,

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:48.131
and I'm gonna release it.

00:01:48.131 --> 00:01:48.964
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:01:48.964 --> 00:01:50.219
- I just don't wanna look
back on my life when I'm 80

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:51.089
and wish I had done it.

00:01:51.089 --> 00:01:52.630
- [Kelly] Regret not going for it.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.463
- Exactly.

00:01:53.463 --> 00:01:54.420
- And it sounds awesome.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.253
- [Alexander] Thank
you so much. Thank you.

00:01:55.253 --> 00:01:57.537
- Yeah, at first I was like,
"Oh, he sings country?"

00:01:57.537 --> 00:01:58.650
And I was like, "Awesome."

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.860
And it wasn't that you were Canadian.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:00.970
Canadians actually love country music.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.310
- Got a huge country
music scene in Canada.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.390
- I toured with Reba,

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.300
and literally it's like crazy up there.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.133
They love it.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:06.966
- Wow.

00:02:06.966 --> 00:02:07.799
- [Kelly] Yeah, I love it.

00:02:07.799 --> 00:02:09.010
- And like the hockey dressing rooms,

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.950
that's what we'd all be
listening to back then.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.783
- That's intense.

00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:14.640
I like country music
'cause there's a story.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.473
- Yeah, yeah, 100%.

00:02:15.473 --> 00:02:16.920
- There's a story they tell ya,

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.649
I'm gonna drive down to the gas station.

00:02:18.649 --> 00:02:19.707
I'm gonna take a left.

00:02:19.707 --> 00:02:21.532
(Alexander laughs)
- My dog's with me.

00:02:21.532 --> 00:02:23.251
- You've got the whole,
- My dog is with me.

00:02:23.251 --> 00:02:24.197
- You've got the thing.

00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:26.040
It's a lot of details.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.359
- He's got some painted-on jeans.

00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:28.500
That's usually one. (laughs)

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.210
Yes, like awesome.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.043
- I got the receipt.

00:02:31.043 --> 00:02:32.860
I need to go return the
gift and get a new one,

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:33.693
and you're like, "Wow."

00:02:33.693 --> 00:02:35.020
- [Alexander] It's very, very practical.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.620
- Painted a picture here.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.360
- I like a picture.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.006
No, but congrats on Vikings.

00:02:40.006 --> 00:02:40.839
- Oh, thank you.

00:02:40.839 --> 00:02:41.900
- Do you just love doing it?

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:42.733
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:02:42.733 --> 00:02:44.600
- Thanks. Thank you.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.870
- Here's the thing I
love about your character

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:47.703
because I had seen it,

00:02:47.703 --> 00:02:49.572
but I had no idea it was
based off a real character,

00:02:49.572 --> 00:02:51.043
like a real life person.

00:02:51.043 --> 00:02:52.180
- [Alexander] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.060
- I didn't know that.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.960
- Björn Ironside was a real live Viking.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:56.940
He was the first king of Sweden,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.170
and he said that he was
the son of Ragnar Lothbrok,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.750
who is kind of a mythological character

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.480
that we don't actually know if he existed.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.430
I'm such a history buff.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.896
I love that kind of stuff.

00:03:04.896 --> 00:03:06.140
- I think it's cool.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:08.170
- And by the way, I just
watched your Netflix special.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.003
You're amazing.

00:03:09.003 --> 00:03:09.836
- Thank you.
- So good.

00:03:09.836 --> 00:03:10.680
(audience applauds)
- We've met before--

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.456
(audience cheering drowns out Alexander).

00:03:12.456 --> 00:03:14.910
- I just realized that, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.785
- Thank you for making this about me.

00:03:16.785 --> 00:03:18.048
- No, it was so good.

00:03:18.048 --> 00:03:20.450
It was so good.
- Thank you. I agree.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.283
- [Kelly] Speaking of Vikings,

00:03:21.283 --> 00:03:22.116
(Alexander laughs)

00:03:22.116 --> 00:03:22.949
- Wait, no, "I agree.

00:03:22.949 --> 00:03:23.782
"I agree. I'm awesome."

00:03:23.782 --> 00:03:24.615
- [Alexander] "Yes, yes, I'm awesome."

00:03:24.615 --> 00:03:26.420
(laughing)

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.600
- So wait, do you think

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.110
that you would actually make a good Viking

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.310
after having to like...

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.340
'cause it's been kinda grueling.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.290
I read how y'all shot this,

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.310
and how you regularly shoot.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.970
It's like crazy hard.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.970
- No, it really was one of
the most trying experiences

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:38.803
of my life.

00:03:38.803 --> 00:03:40.030
No, I would make a terrible Viking.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.550
I mean, it's not for
divas, that's for sure.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.193
But it was a great experience.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.103
I have a story.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.070
They put a ton of makeup on
you and try to break you down

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.025
for the show.
- Welcome to being a woman

00:03:52.025 --> 00:03:52.858
all the time.

00:03:52.858 --> 00:03:54.889
(laughing)
- Welcome to being a woman.

00:03:54.889 --> 00:03:55.722
- You know what?

00:03:55.722 --> 00:03:56.593
It doesn't look like this, okay?

00:03:56.593 --> 00:03:59.636
- [Whitney] No idea what that's like.

00:03:59.636 --> 00:04:00.469
- That's a lot.

00:04:00.469 --> 00:04:01.302
(Kelly talking drowns out Alexander)

00:04:01.302 --> 00:04:03.600
- And there's times where,

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.160
just because it's so quick and demanding,

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.630
that you don't have time to put on makeup.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.630
I'll never forget this one time.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.091
I went down.

00:04:09.091 --> 00:04:10.080
I was like, "Screw it.
I'm gonna do it myself."

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.930
And I just pull out this big clod of dirt,

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.460
and I stuck it all over my face,

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.741
and I realize after, it was horse (beep).

00:04:15.741 --> 00:04:18.225
(audience gasps and groans)

00:04:18.225 --> 00:04:19.058
- [Alexander] And I'm like,

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.570
- Oh, that is--
- That has been my life

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.766
for six years.

00:04:22.766 --> 00:04:27.723
- That is the greatest story
I've ever heard on this show.

00:04:27.723 --> 00:04:28.923
(audience applauds)

00:04:28.923 --> 00:04:29.756
- Yeah.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.663
Did you vomit?

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.060
- I didn't have time to take it off,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.078
so I just--
- Oh my god!

00:04:37.078 --> 00:04:38.810
- Just went through with it.
- Oh my god!

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.702
- By the way, your skin looks amazing.

00:04:40.702 --> 00:04:42.982
(Alexander laughs)

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.619
- [Kelly] Maybe we should try it.

00:04:44.619 --> 00:04:45.452
- I don't know.

00:04:45.452 --> 00:04:46.285
- Hey, Shark Tank.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.270
- I think there's a business here.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.220
- Shark Tank, another gift to give you.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.504
That's horri... You're very method.

00:04:52.504 --> 00:04:53.337
(laughing)

